# Manual companion to the executable Newman Security proof folder.
# Requires tasks 10, 11, 15, 16 and 19-21. Use a disposable database.
# Obtain tokens and a real CustomerA order with the Newman setup or generated.http.
# Replace placeholders locally. Never commit tokens or credentials.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@customerAToken = REPLACE_LOCALLY
@customerBToken = REPLACE_LOCALLY
@adminToken = REPLACE_LOCALLY
@orderId = REPLACE_WITH_CUSTOMERA_ORDER_UUID
@statusBody = REPLACE_WITH_VALID_TASK21_JSON

### Establish that the resource exists for its owner: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}

### Required proof 1 - another customer gets 404 Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerBToken}}

### Admin can read that same resource: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Required proof 2 - owner is a Customer and gets 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{statusBody}}

### Read again as the owner and compare with the first response: unchanged
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}

### Anonymous access gets 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### Unknown URL API version gets 404 Problem Details
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v999/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"unused@shop.test","password":"Example123!"}
